  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of such an outcome. In this case, Lottery A has a 100% chance of avoiding a large loss (if -5 is acceptable), while Lottery B has a 99.9% chance. The reason would slightly favor A. The individual in the report does consider the low probability of loss in Lottery B and acknowledges the small loss in the other lottery. However, there is no indication that the decision was driven by a rule that prioritizes higher probability of favorable outcomes. The individual notes the low risk in B but does not conclude that higher probability of a favorable outcome makes B (or A) better. The reasoning is observational rather than rule-based. There is no evidence of applying a comparative probability rule to justify the choice. Therefore, while probability is mentioned, the specific reasoning pattern of the decision reason is not clearly present.",
